      "content": "Exactly. Squaring both sides gives\n\\[\nx+28=(2-x)^2 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x^2-5x-24=0\n\\]\n\\[\n(x-8)(x+3)=0 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=8\\text{ or }x=-3.\n\\]\nCheck them in the original equation: $x=8$ gives $6\\ne-6$, so it is not valid. For $x=-3$, both sides equal $5$. Therefore, $\\boxed{x=-3}$; $x=8$ is rejected."
